  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the shortest distance between the point $(5,-1)$ and the line $y=2.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934287/assets/f907ee8b0bb92792cc69905678210af71088af6731e5a586eaeed0bfc7856b9c.png)\n\nSince the line $y=2$ is a horizontal line, the shortest distance between this line and the point $(5,-1)$ is given by the absolute value of the difference between $y$-coordinate of the point and $2.$ \n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=|-1-2|=3.\n$$",
